    "custom_faq_afKPpE": {
      "type": "custom-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_73nVbP": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q1. What Makes This 4.4× Stronger?",
            "answer": "<p>Most standard fish oil supplements typically provide around<strong>180 mg EPA + 120 mg DHA per gram (approximately 300 mg total Omega-3 actives)</strong>. Our formulation delivers<strong>up to 800 mg EPA + 600 mg DHA per daily serving (1400 mg total EPA+DHA)</strong>, providing<strong>approximately 4.4× more Omega-3 actives</strong>compared to conventional fish oil formulations. This means<strong>higher EPA and DHA concentration in fewer softgels</strong>, helping deliver more nutritional value per serving.<br/><br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_AiC3Cc": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q2. Does It Help Triglyceride Levels?",
            "answer": "<p>Omega-3 fatty acids, particularly<strong>EPA</strong>, have been extensively studied for their role in supporting<strong>healthy triglyceride levels and cardiovascular health</strong>. Higher EPA intake has been associated with improved lipid metabolism and may help maintain triglycerides already within the normal range when combined with a healthy lifestyle.<br/><br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_TpFhPg": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q3. Will it Help With Brain Fog And Focus?",
            "answer": "<p><strong>DHA is one of the major structural fats found in the brain and nervous system.</strong>Adequate DHA intake supports neuronal membrane function, cognitive performance, memory, and mental clarity. Regular Omega-3 intake may help support focus and overall cognitive wellness.<br/><br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_3hkBR6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q4. Why Include Tocotrienols?",
            "answer": "<p>This formula includes<strong>Tocotrienols, an advanced form of Vitamin E</strong>, sourced for their powerful antioxidant properties. Tocotrienols help protect cells from oxidative stress and complement Omega-3s by supporting<strong>antioxidant defence, cardiovascular wellness, and healthy lipid metabolism</strong>.<br/><br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_EQhRt4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q5. Does It Reduce Joint Inflammation?",
            "answer": "<p>Omega-3 fatty acids, especially<strong>EPA</strong>, are known to support a<strong>healthy inflammatory response</strong>in the body. Regular supplementation may help promote<strong>joint comfort, flexibility, and mobility</strong>, making it beneficial for active individuals and those experiencing everyday joint stiffness.<br/><br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_FbLgJ3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q6. Is enteric coating important?",
            "answer": "<p>Our softgels feature <strong>enteric coating</strong>, which helps prevent the capsule from breaking down in the stomach. This allows Omega-3s to be released further in the digestive tract, helping reduce <strong>fishy burps, aftertaste, and stomach discomfort</strong>, while improving overall tolerance.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_mfEYKK": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q7. Can pregnant women use Omega-3?",
            "answer": "<p>Omega-3s, especially<strong>DHA</strong>, play an important nutritional role during pregnancy and are widely used to support maternal and fetal nutrition. However,<strong>pregnant or breastfeeding women should consult their physician before use</strong>to determine the appropriate dosage for their individual needs.<br/><br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_Xg8n8N": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q8. Does This Help Dry Skin?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Omega-3 fatty acids help support the <strong>skin barrier, hydration, and overall skin health</strong>. They contribute to maintaining skin moisture and may help support healthy-looking skin by promoting a balanced inflammatory response. The research behind Omega-3s also highlights their role in supporting skin structure and hydration.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_DeM9aj": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q9. How Long To See Cholesterol Benefits?",
            "answer": "<p>Omega-3 benefits build gradually with consistent use. Most studies evaluating lipid and metabolic support generally assess outcomes over <strong>8–12 weeks of daily supplementation</strong>, alongside a balanced diet and healthy lifestyle.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_ECQynf": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q10. Is This Sustainably Sourced?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Our Omega-3 is sourced from <strong>premium-quality global suppliers</strong> selected for quality, purity, and ingredient standards. Every batch is manufactured under strict quality controls to ensure consistency and reliability.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        }
      },
